  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Category Standard, Played Straight",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Category Standard, Played Straight\"**\n\nTempah looks like the booking tool you already trust: neutral greys, white surfaces, hairline edges, and one confident blue that marks what you can press and what you've chosen. It refuses ornament on purpose. The quality is in the craft (exact radii, borders that never shift layout, thumb-sized targets, a calm loss screen) rather than in any brand flourish. The bar is Cal.com and Stripe.\n\nThe business leads; Tempah does not. A shop's page opens on the shop's name and initials, and Tempah appears only as a small \"Bookings by Tempah\" credit at the foot of the page. Density is moderate and phone-first: one column at the thumb on a phone, a bordered booker card from tablet up.\n\nConfirmed rejections: purple or violet anywhere, the shadcn-default stacked-card look with a tinted brand, and the generic AI-generated aesthetic (gradients as decoration, glass, glow).",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One blue for action, selection and focus; everything else neutral.",
      "Status colour is single-purpose: red means a slot was taken, green means booked.",
      "Borders are inset shadows, so a 2px selected edge never moves a pixel of content.",
      "Every public-page target is at least 44px tall.",
      "Motion is nearly absent: 150ms colour and edge fades, one slide-in."
